   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the exact value of \\( \\sum_{n=2}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n^{2}-1} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         3,
         4
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Partial fractions give \\( \\frac{1}{n^{2}-1} = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{n-1} - \\frac{1}{n+1}\\right) \\), so the series telescopes.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Divide",
               1,
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  [
                     "Add",
                     "n",
                     -1
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  1,
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     2,
                     [
                        "Add",
                        "n",
                        1
                     ]
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Writing out the terms from \\( n = 2 \\) to \\( n = N \\), the inner terms cancel and the partial sum is \\( S_N = \\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{1}{2 \\left(N + 1\\right)} - \\frac{1}{2 N} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Rational",
               3,
               4
            ],
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  1,
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     2,
                     "N"
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  1,
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     2,
                     [
                        "Add",
                        "N",
                        1
                     ]
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "As \\( N \\to \\infty \\), the terms containing \\( N \\) approach their limits, so \\( \\lim_{N \\to \\infty} S_N = \\frac{3}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The value of the series is \\( \\frac{3}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            4
         ]
      }
